<item>
            <title>[LU-20501] sanityn test_102: ZFS check_fhandle_syscalls d102.sanityn.stripe/subdir fail, open_by_handle_at error: Stale file handle</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20501</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Andreas Dilger &amp;lt;adilger@dilger.ca&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2f2b278e-90e9-4d08-b762-0cdd443121f4&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2f2b278e-90e9-4d08-b762-0cdd443121f4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_102 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;open_by_handle_at(subdir) error: Stale file handle
check_fhandle_syscalls d102.sanityn.stripe/subdir fail
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;br/&gt;
clients: &lt;a href=&quot;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127450&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127450&lt;/a&gt; - 5.14.0-611.55.1.el9_7.x86_64&lt;br/&gt;
servers: &lt;a href=&quot;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127450&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127450&lt;/a&gt; - 5.14.0-611.55.1.el9_7_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This started failing again intermittently for ZFS after it was re-enabled for all testing.  48 failures since it was enabled on 2026-07-06 when patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/66226&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66226&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15757&quot; title=&quot;sanityn test_109: Oops in ll_md_blocking_ast() at umount&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15757&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15757&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: re-enable sanityn/102 after fix&quot;) landed, and 27/286 ~= 10% for master ZFS test sessions in the past week.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unlike &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15757&quot; title=&quot;sanityn test_109: Oops in ll_md_blocking_ast() at umount&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15757&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15757&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; this is no longer crashing the client, but there is still something wrong with the osd-zfs code.  There are no failures with osd-ldiskfs.&lt;/p&gt;







&lt;p&gt;VVVVVVV DO NOT REMOVE LINES BELOW, Added by Maloo for auto-association VVVVVVV&lt;br/&gt;
sanityn test_102 - check_fhandle_syscalls d102.sanityn.stripe/subdir fail&lt;/p&gt;</description>
